			)
			(property "Description" "Texas Instruments TPS7A0233 nanopower-IQ 200mA low-dropout linear regulator, fixed 3.3V output, SOT-23-5 (DBV). Chosen 2026-09-23 to replace the MCP1700T-3302E/TT on this board: quiescent current drops from 1.6uA typ / 4uA max to 25nA typ / 46nA max at 25C (60nA max over -40..85C), which matters because the wristband spends most of its life asleep and the LDO was the single largest standby draw. Shutdown IQ 3nA. VIN 1.5-6.0V, output accuracy +/-1.5% over temperature, dropout 270mV max at 200mA (this board draws 45mA worst case), current limit 450mA typ, PSRR 55dB at 1kHz, output noise 130uVrms, UVLO 1.3V rising. Requires CIN 1uF and COUT 1uF nominal with at least 0.5uF EFFECTIVE output capacitance for stability (22uF derated max). NOTE the EN pin has an internal pulldown and the device is DISABLED when EN floats -- EN must be driven high; on this board it is tied to VBAT, since the MCU this rail powers cannot enable its own supply. All pin and electrical data verified directly against the real TI data sheet SBVS277C (Table 5-1 'Pin Functions', Figure 5-2 'DBV Package, 5-Pin SOT-23', Section 6.3 'Recommended Operating Conditions', Section 6.5 'Electrical Characteristics')."
				(at 0 0 0)
				(show_name no)
				(do_not_autoplace no)
				(hide yes)
				(effects
					(font
						(size 1.27 1.27)
					)
				)
			)
